      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "HOLD THE DOOR (2) has yet to make his mark in 2 starts since being brought out of Sydney late last season. He should be at his peak fitness third up, and with another drop in class, he is set to show some worthwhile form, especially with the step up to 1600m. NORTHERN CHILD (4) steps out to 1600m third up from a spell, and his first 2 starts back have been satisfactory. Anthony Darmanin sticks with him, and so do we. Keep him safe in all combos. TIMELY NEEDS (3) races best on this circuit and followed up an overdue maiden win at his penultimate start with a fair fourth of 6 in class 2 company here 3 weeks ago. He slides back in class and can bounce straight back into the money. TIME FOR SNOW (5) has also recently been bought out of Sydney, and his 2 local starts have had some merit. The extra 200m is ideal, and he is also a top 4 chance in an even contest. PITMAN (7) has trekked over from the mainland with Patrick Kearney and is ready to put his best hoof forward third up. Include.",
